cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "SOCE Codebook v0.1 and Corpus Registry"
abstract: >-
  Measurement canon for SOCE (Social-Ontological Cycle of Exclusion), a
  five-node diagnostic architecture for reading how contemporary democracies
  naturalise the exclusion of the Other. This deposit contains the codebook
  (ordinal rubrics for node states, Todorov axes and inter-node link states),
  the anchor set, and the registry of documented corpus cases. Notation is
  qualitative-ordinal throughout: ordinal states are never averaged, summed or
  weighted. Reproducibility is defined as two independent analysts producing
  the same structural signature, not as a statistical coefficient. Exploratory
  use is open; canonical diagnosis requires two trained coders under the
  delta-protocol.

